 "rules": "(written before any grade-wise tabulation of this script's output; the earlier AI-assisted audit\nresults/a_audit_links.json had been read). Precedence: conflicting > unresolved > record-consistent. \"Confirmed\" does not\nexist: the register cannot establish who uses a meter.\n  conflicting, if any of\n    C1 name_status == other          (some register / address-search name exists, none contains the facility's proper name\n                                      or its facility-type word)\n    C2 name_on_other_title           (the matched title has a name without the proper name while another title on the\n                                      parcel carries it: the link chose another building of the parcel)\n    C3 use_status == conflict        (facility type known, register main use outside the s02_link.USE_OK list)\n    C4 area_status == outside        (register area outside +/-30% of both area values of the project record)\n  unresolved, if no conflict and any of\n    U1 n_main_titles != 1            (several main buildings share the parcel meter, or none is recorded)\n    U2 collective                    (collective register or address-search building kind 1 = apartment complex)\n    U3 name_status in {blank, type_only}\n    U4 area_status in {footprint_only, no_project_area}\n    U5 use_status == facility_type_other\n  record-consistent otherwise: one main title, proper name found, use compatible, area within +/-30% of the project GFA.\nEvidence recorded but not used in the class: attached-building titles, administrative-code change, energy-response fields.\nThe class overlaps with the grade by construction (grade A already requires one main title, use and area agreement), so\nwithin grade A only the name and the footprint-only area can move a building out of record-consistent.",
